---
title: Salted peanut butter cookies
servings: 12
yield: 12 large or 24 small cookies
tags: [gluten-free, dairy-free]
source: Salted Peanut Butter Cookies (Gluten-Free & Dairy-Free) by Ovenly, https://www.oven.ly/recipes/project-one-ephnc-78ycr
---

Heat the oven to 350°F and line a #rimmed sheet pan{} with parchment.

In a #medium bowl{}, whisk the @light brown sugar{1 3/4%cup} and @eggs{2}(room temperature) hard until combined. Whisk in the @vanilla extract{1/2%tsp}.

Add the @peanut butter{1 3/4%cup} and stir with a spatula until smooth, with no streaks left. It should feel like modelling clay.

Shape into 12 balls of about 2 inches (2 to 2 1/4 oz each), or heaped tablespoons for small cookies, and set them on the pan.

> They hold their shape better if frozen ~{15%minutes} before baking.

Sprinkle lightly with @coarse salt{} and bake ~{20%minutes} to 22 minutes (small ones ~{16%minutes} to 18), turning the pan halfway. They are done when lightly golden and cracked on top. Cool completely.
